  data: {
    LLM: "Each round establishes dominant rank and usually a dominant suit through bidding. Declarers take the kitty and discard back to kitty size. Trick play then proceeds with strict follow/combination constraints based on lead pattern and trump structure. Opponents' captured point cards (5s, 10s, Kings) determine whether declarers keep deal and advance or defenders seize momentum.",
    Player: "Each round establishes dominant rank and usually a dominant suit through bidding. Declarers take the kitty and discard back to kitty size. Trick play then proceeds with strict follow/combination constraints based on lead pattern and trump structure. Opponents' captured point cards (5s, 10s, Kings) determine whether declarers keep deal and advance or defenders seize momentum.",
    objective: "Raise your partnership rank from 2 upward (often to Ace) by winning rounds while controlling opponents' trick points.",
    gameplay: "Each round establishes dominant rank and usually a dominant suit through bidding. Declarers take the kitty and discard back to kitty size. Trick play then proceeds with strict follow/combination constraints based on lead pattern and trump structure. Opponents' captured point cards (5s, 10s, Kings) determine whether declarers keep deal and advance or defenders seize momentum.",
    keyRules: [
      'Dynamic trump rank each round changes comparative card power.',
      'Only 5s, 10s, and Kings score points in tricks.',
      "Round control shifts based on opponents' point total thresholds.",
