      "Rule example: Raise your partnership rank from 2 upward (often to Ace) by winning rounds while controlling opponents' trick points.",
      "Turn-flow example: Each round establishes dominant rank and usually a dominant suit through bidding. Declarers take the kitty and discard back to kitty size. Trick play then proceeds with strict follow/combination constraints based on lead pattern and trump structure. Opponents' captured point cards (5s, 10s, Kings) determine whether declarers keep deal and advance or defenders seize momentum.",
      "Scoring example: Only point cards score in tricks: 5s, 10s, and Kings. Round outcomes and level advancement depend on opponents' total captured points and variant thresholds. Advance your partnership rank above the agreed target (commonly from 2 toward Ace) before opponents do..",
